import QtslAux.Sweep.Discrete

/-! # The `Repulse100` benchmark row

Machine-generated theorem file internalizing a certified reachability bound for the `Repulse100`
benchmark system as a Lean-checked consequence of its certificate.

The system is a random walk on `ℤ`: while the state lies in `[0, 100]`, each step moves by `-2` or
`+1` with probability `1/2` each; all other states are absorbing. The certificate is the
exact-rational table `tbl`, packaged as the supermartingale witness `V`; its bounds, barrier, and
drift conditions are verified by `norm_num`-level rational arithmetic and discharged through
`Sweep.reach_le_of_battery`.

* `sound`: starting from `10`, the probability that the walk ever reaches `101` or beyond is at
  most the certificate value at the initial state, stated as an exact rational;
* `sound_dec`: the same bound relaxed to the decimal bound
  `0.00000000000000000009555617022121990013692121588544546389601705400`.
-/

